    example: "In Acts 15 the apostles and elders debated whether Gentile believers must be circumcised. They listened to Peter’s experience, to Paul and Barnabas, and to Scripture (Amos 9:11-12), then concluded, ‘it seemed good to the Holy Spirit, and to us’ (Acts 15:28). Interpretation was a shared, Spirit-led process.",
